@startuml account-status
!include ../_theme.puml
title Account status (EAccountStatus)

' Derived from: wovely models/EAccountStatus, models/User#effectiveStatus, services/UserPenaltyService,
' security/services/UserDetailsImpl#isAccountNonLocked, services/RefreshTokenService#revokeAll, services/UserQueryService
hide empty description

[*] --> ACTIVE : sign-up

ACTIVE --> SUSPENDED : admin penalty\nsuspendDays 1..365 (required)
ACTIVE --> BANNED : admin penalty
SUSPENDED --> ACTIVE : admin restores
SUSPENDED --> ACTIVE : suspendedUntil passes\n(liftExpiredSuspensions, every 5 min)
SUSPENDED --> BANNED : admin penalty
BANNED --> ACTIVE : admin restores
BANNED --> SUSPENDED : admin penalty

ACTIVE : strikes +1 on STRIKE (status unchanged)
SUSPENDED : on entry: revokeAll(refresh tokens)
SUSPENDED : locked until suspendedUntil
BANNED : on entry: revokeAll(refresh tokens)
BANNED : always locked, no end date

note right of SUSPENDED
  Between the end date and the next job run,
  login, the CRM and its status filter already
  treat the account as ACTIVE (effective status).
  Legacy records without an end date stay locked
  until an admin restores them (fail closed).
end note
@enduml
